@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] web-domain-authority
User-visible machine and terminal operations MUST call the corresponding Ash
domain with the authenticated actor. Hidden controls, client-supplied roles or
cached permission flags MUST NOT replace current domain/Cedar authorization.
Provisioner requests use the separate authenticated host coordinators.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] web-current-login
Authenticated machine and terminal LiveViews MUST verify the stored login at
mount and before every event, parameter change and refresh. Revoked or expired
logins MUST halt the operation and redirect to sign-in. A mounted actor alone
MUST NOT remain sufficient authority. See ADR-0022.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] web-sensitive-diagnostics
Authentication paths and terminal processes MUST be tagged for privacy before
diagnostics can expose tokens, terminal bytes or process state. Error replies
MUST NOT include credentials, raw database errors or terminal payloads.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] web-bounded-domain-views
Machine and sharing lists MUST consume bounded domain pages and replace the
displayed LiveView streams on refresh. Web code MUST NOT bypass pagination with
unbounded resource reads or retain every previously visited page in assigns.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product] installer-only-ssh-setup
Machine connection controls MUST retain the Overalls installation and SSH commands
for eligible machines. Marshall Web MUST NOT offer or serve per-machine SSH
configuration downloads; the public installer and Lyra's local setup remain the
supported configuration path.
